  "review_conclusions": [
    "Package-lock DTO deserialization checks wire shape; consumers must still validate identity,target,authority,capacity and canonical selection ordering. Canonicalization clones and sorts rather than mutating the source DTO.",
    "Shared package-lock SHA-256 includes schema,target,authority and entries while intentionally excluding checkout-local project GUID and manifest digest; consumers compare that excluded identity separately. No digest is proof of host authorization.",
    "ProjectLaunchIntent constructors and custom Deserialize centralize version/name/path-shape checks. Owned path input is not filesystem resolution,existence,canonical root identity,profile admission or authentication. Retarget preserves operation/source/profile while validating a new requested open path.",
    "Retired reference migration first iteratively admits the full tree with inclusive node/depth/reference budgets,then rewrites exact legacy shapes. Budget rejection happens before resolver callbacks; later parse/resolver errors do not roll back earlier callback effects. The single-reference adapter has a different scope from whole-tree admission.",
    "The V2 session codec bounds UTF-8 bytes and rejects missing,duplicate,unknown,old-version or invalid fields before returning an owned record. It does not acquire an OS lease.",
    "The admission record validates nonzero epoch,instance token syntax and lifecycle/generation combinations. Only Activating can commit_ready; Closing/Recovery may retain a committed generation. Heartbeat replacement neither increments epoch nor enforces monotonic timestamps.",
    "Windows mutex naming hashes the supplied path's UTF-16LE representation. Record existence,Ready status and a heartbeat alone cannot prove an active platform lease. Hub and Editor use different normalization adapters; current evidence does not prove different final mutex names,so CR-PROJECT-0004 remains a TODO.",
    "Two existing struct-variant layouts fail rustfmt --check. Every original raw byte is preserved and both files parse under stdout-only rustfmt. The other14 exact paths pass; no automatic formatting or Cargo/Rust tests ran."
  ],
